<title>UK: CRICKET-AUSTRALIA CRUMBLE TO LEATHERDALE.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-AUSTRALIA CRUMBLE TO LEATHERDALE.</headline>
<dateline>WORCESTER, England 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia crumbled to</p>
<p>121 all out in 35 overs against Worcestershire on Sunday in the</p>
<p>third match of their Ashes tour.</p>
<p>On a morning made for seamers, David Leatherdale polished</p>
<p>off the tail to end with five for 10 in five overs.</p>
<p>Gavin Haynes (4-40) had struck among the top order</p>
<p>including Greg Blewett for 22 and Steve Waugh for 21, but at</p>
<p>104-4 Australia seemed in fair shape only to fold dramatically.</p>
<p>At lunch, Worcestershire were 20-0 after 13 overs.</p>
<p>Australia have won their previous two one-dayers, against</p>
<p>Northamptonshire and the Duke of Norfolk's X1. The international</p>
<p>one-day series against England starts on Thursday.</p>
</text>
